Harvey Weinstein fire from his own  company et has the statement released by  The Weinstein Company Board of  Representatives on Sunday it reads in  part quote in light of new information  about misconduct by Harvey Weinstein  that has emerged in the past few days  the directors of The Weinstein Company  have determined and have informed Harvey  Weinstein that his employment with the  Weinstein Company is terminated  effective immediately Weinstein's firing  comes on the heels of an explosive  report published in The New York Times  on Thursday the studio head was accused  of three decades of sexual harassment by  actress Ashley Judd and more women in  Hollywood in a statement to ET on  Thursday Weinstein's lawyer Charles J  harder called the New York Times report  saturated with false and defamatory  statements harder also added that  Weinstein is planning to file a lawsuit  all proceeds will be donated to women's  organizations a New York Times  spokesperson said the publication stands  by its reporting the article also claims  that the film mogul has reached eight  settlements with women over sexual  harassment claims from 1990 to 2015  additionally Weinstein issued a lengthy  apology on Thursday he said he's working  with therapists and taking a leave of  absence from his company to deal with  his issues he said in part quote I  appreciate the way I've behaved with  colleagues in the past has caused a lot  of pain and I sincerely apologize for it  though I'm trying to do better I know I  have a long way to go a former employee  at The Weinstein Company who wished to  remain anonymous tells et the  accusations against Weinstein are  nothing new adding they don't think  anything will change
 

